        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"243791\">David Renshaw</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Kernel.20Reduction.20Visualization/near/618995540\">said</a> in <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"270676\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Kernel.20Reduction.20Visualization/with/618995904\">#lean4 &gt; Kernel Reduction Visualization</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My branch is <a href=\"https://github.com/dwrensha/lean4lean/tree/reduce-cmd\">https://github.com/dwrensha/lean4lean/tree/reduce-cmd</a>. It just does the bare minimum to get the animation in the video to work, and it's still on leanprover/lean4:v4.4.0-rc1.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Oh, what a shame</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't know how much work would be required to get this working on a newer Lean version. It's possible that it would be easier to use an alternate kernel implementation like Nanoda.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I have found <a href=\"https://github.com/ammkrn/nanoda_lib\">Nanoda</a>. And it would take me a while to configure it out since it uses Rust</p>",
